WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.190
All right.

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:02.190
So, yes, we have to talk about it.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.250
The Donald Trump's health story has gone mainstream.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:11.349
And I want to be really careful with this
story because Donald Trump is denying something

00:00:11.349 --> 00:00:16.900
that has not actually been alleged and that
is extremely suspicious.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.680
But I don't want to be alleging that thing.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.430
I think you're going to understand momentarily
here.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:28.390
So over the last several years, there have
been general health concerns about the president.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:30.340
What's going on with his cognitive state?

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:34.499
You've got these twitches and spasms that
coincide with verbal glitches.

00:00:34.499 --> 00:00:37.690
You sometimes have upper trump and sometimes
down or Trump.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.739
He often seems confused.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:43.449
He sometimes slurs without a real explanation.

00:00:43.449 --> 00:00:46.559
We've seen him dragging his right leg while
walking.

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:51.969
We've seen Donald Trump sort of unable to
just speak normally, talking about the oranges

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:55.530
of an investigation and so on and so forth.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:01:01.389
And then we had in 2019 that abrupt visit
to Walter Reed Hospital, which we were told

00:01:01.389 --> 00:01:08.090
was merely Trump deciding on on a weekend
that he had a few extra hours in his day.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:13.300
So he would show up at Walter Reed and get
a jump on when he didn't pass the sniff test

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.370
at the time.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:19.720
Well, there is a new book coming from New
York Times reporter Michael Schmidt, which

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:27.230
says that visit to Walter Reed was not Trump,
saying, let's get a jump on my physical.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:34.420
That it was some kind of abrupt visit due
to something medical that happened with Donald

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.420
Trump.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:40.460
And it was serious enough that Vice President
Mike Pence was told Trump may need to be put

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:46.940
under anesthesia, be on standby in case you
need to take over for some period of time.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.580
Those are the allegations from Michael Schmidt.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:54.540
So these suspicions always were Trump wasn't
there for his physical and the book claims

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.830
to corroborate that.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:02:00.360
Now, this would not be typical if Donald.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:05.050
It wouldn't be typical for Mike Pence to be
put on standby in case Trump has to be put

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:06.710
under anesthesia.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:11.520
If Trump's really going for a physical, that
wouldn't be normal for a physical.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.040
So that's so far OK.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:18.500
There's been an allegation made that that
visit was was it some kind of medical incident?

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:23.950
Donald Trump tweets out of nowhere that he
hasn't suffered mini strokes.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:28.060
Now, you might say, why is Trump tweeting
about mini strokes?

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.970
Michael Schmidt didn't say anything about
mini strokes.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:31.240
Well, that's exactly the question.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.130
Donald Trump tweeting, quote, It never ends.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:39.800
Now they are trying to say that your favorite
president, me, went to Walter Reed Medical

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:46.720
Center, having suffered a series of mini strokes,
never happened to this candidate.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.480
Fake news, perhaps they are referring to another
candidate from another party.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.540
Now, this is this information.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.910
It has not been alleged that Trump has been
suffering many strokes.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.270
Let me be clear.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:00.800
People on Twitter have alleged it.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:06.150
But the point is, it is not part of Michael
Schmidt's forthcoming book that Trump suffered

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.270
mini strokes.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:12.430
Trump is out of nowhere saying that something
didn't happen, which no one has alleged.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:17.290
This would be like if someone went to the
hospital and you say, hey, did did you go

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:21.130
to the hospital for routine blood work or
did something happen?

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.270
And you say, I didn't have a heart attack.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.200
I definitely didn't have a heart attack.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:29.450
It would raise suspicion if you start denying
something that wasn't alleged.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:32.140
And in fact, it raises more questions than
it answers.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:38.060
Now, I got an e-mail from Daniel, who's a
viewer who says, my mother is a board certified

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:39.200
neurologist.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.099
I showed her a few clips of Trump's foot dragging,
slurred speech, etc. and she was fairly certain

00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:48.690
he had a mild stroke recently, possibly the
night he was rushed to Walter Reed Hospital.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:56.200
So when presented with some of the video of
Trump, you can certainly find medical professionals

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.900
who would who would ask about something like
a stroke.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.650
But it is not actually what the book alleges.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:08.310
Now, we also regularly see video, as is mentioned
in the email, of Donald Trump walking and

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:12.739
kind of dragging his right foot, not picking
it up completely as he walks.

00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:18.600
It is true that such video exists, but again,
it is not proof of anything.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:20.350
So here's my take on this.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:25.230
We should be careful not to claim anything
happened when we don't know that it did.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.230
Yes.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:29.220
The visit to Walter Reed was weird.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:30.220
Yes.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:34.380
It never passed the sniff test that Trump
was getting ahead on his 20/20 physical.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.380
Yes.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:41.570
Trump bringing up strokes when they haven't
been mentioned is extraordinarily odd.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:46.880
But we really need to get actual answers about
why Donald Trump went to the hospital.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:52.630
And if it was for a physical, there would
be no reason that he would be placed under

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:53.630
a..

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:57.710
That that he would be expected to go under
anesthesia and there would be no reason for

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:00.870
Mike Pence to be told be at the ready.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:06.310
So it is gaslighting for Trump to deny having
a stroke because it hasn't been alleged.

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:13.050
And yet it is suspicious that Trump is focusing
in on strokes, particularly since it's not

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:14.330
something that has been mentioned.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:21.310
So it would be great if at some point, because
I do think that as a general principle, the

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:26.910
voting public has a right to know about the
real health status of people who may be arguably

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:31.220
the most powerful people in the world or among
them.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:33.510
I do think the public has a right to know.

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:37.120
And the White House should just come clean
about the reason for that visit.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:43.440
Adding fuel to the fire of suspicion is that
when asked about this Mike Pence, his answer

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:48.580
was, it was certainly squirrely, slippery.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:49.790
Let me put it that way.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:51.270
And that's what I want to talk about next

